# Moxa ioLogik E2240.
# Converted automatically from the Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST); see ATTRIBUTION.md.
# Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation.
# Corrections are welcome (CONTRIBUTING.md). Remove @x_status once this table has been checked against the manual.
# | Moxa ioLogik E2240 Ethernet Remote I/O — 8-channel AI + 2-channel AO
# | 
# | Source: ioLogik E2200 Series User Manual Edition 7.0, September 2018 (Appendix I)
# | Protocol: Modbus/TCP port 502
# | 
# | FC03 (4xxxx R/W): AO + AI configuration registers (primary space below)
# | FC04 (3xxxx R): AI values — raw ch0-7 (0x0280-0x0287), min raw (0x0290-0x0297),
# | max raw (0x02A0-0x02A7), scale value f32 step-2 (0x02B0-0x02BF),
# | min scale value f32 step-2 (0x02C0-0x02CF), max scale value f32 step-2 (0x02D0-0x02DF)
# | FC01 (0xxxx R/W): AO channel output clear (write 1 to clear)
# | 
# | NOTE: AI RAW max block starts at 0x01A0 (ref 40417), NOT 0x00A0 — documented gap in address space.
@mbmap=1
@vendor=Moxa
@model=ioLogik E2240
@vendor_website=moxa.com
@description=8-AI + 2-AO Modbus/TCP Ethernet remote I/O (port 502). FC03: AO_value ch0-1 (0-1, 0-4095), AO_powerOnValue ch0-1 (2-3), AO_safeValue ch0-1 (4-5), AO_range ch0-1 (6-7, 0=0-10V 1=4-20mA), AO_powerOnRange ch0-1 (8-9), AO_safeRange ch0-1 (10-11), AI_range ch0-7 (12-19, 0=+/-150mV 1=+/-500mV 2=+/-5V 3=+/-10V 4=0-20mA 5=4-20mA), AI_powerOnRange ch0-7 (20-27), AI_safeRange ch0-7 (28-35), AI_scalingEnable ch0-7 (136-143), AI_rawMin u32 hi+lo ch0-7 (144-159), AI_rawMax u32 hi+lo ch0-7 (0x01A0-0x01AF=416-431; gap from 0x009F to 0x01A0), AI_scaleMin u32 hi+lo ch0-7 (432-447), AI_scaleMax u32 hi+lo ch0-7 (448-463), AI_scaleValue f32 hi+lo ch0-7 (0x0100-0x010F=256-271), IntReg00-23 working (0x0150-0x0167=336-359). FC04: AI_rawValue ch0-7, AI_rawValueMin, AI_rawValueMax, AI_scaleValue f32 step-2, AI_scaleValueMin f32 step-2, AI_scaleValueMax f32 step-2.
@source=Omni Console device library (OmniCoreST), modbus-library/moxa-iologik-e2240.toml; Source: ioLogik E2200 Series User Manual Edition 7.0, September 2018 (Appendix I). Not verified against the manufacturer's documentation
